{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021480-actual-play-chronicles-of-darkness-n\u00e4rwick","id":1021480,"title":"[Actual Play] Chronicles of Darkness: N\u00e4rwick","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-23T22:47:50-08:00","id":1021480,"title":"[Actual Play] Chronicles of Darkness: N\u00e4rwick","content":"<span style=\"font-size:26px\">Chronicles of Darkness: N\u00e4rwick</span><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/narwick/images/c/c6/ClickHandler.ashx.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/300?cb=20120717094713\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <i>N\u00e4rwick is a city that appears on no map, is taught about in no mundane school, and is not even heard about except by its natives and those very few that find their way there through sheer luck and chance. None that are born there ever dream of leaving, and no visitor has ever found it a second time upon leaving. The town seems to be self-sufficient in resources, and always manages to get whatever else it might need. While the locals are as ignorant as anywhere else, most have some idea that the area's an outlier of some kind, as the number of &quot;natural disasters&quot;, &quot;animal attacks&quot;, and simple odd happenstances occurring within are difficult to completely dismiss.</i><br /> <i>The supernatural is everywhere, in a way. A powerful Nexus in the city's center, currently held in check by a local Conspiracy of Hunters, causes otherworldly realms to drift closer to the mundane world; the Gauntlet is thinner, Avernian Gates are plentiful, and energy sources seem to flare into existence continually while dying out more slowly. The Kindred, Werewolves, Beasts, and other creatures of the night tied to this realm, however, are not so nearly numerous as the ghosts, spirits, and angels that so easily find their way into the city's borders, nor the Hunters keeping things from going too far. A minor accord has been formed, a simple council that does little more than keep the Masquerade/Veil in check and make sure the denizens of the town never escalate to all out war with each other (as well as to avoid the focus of the Hunters), but there's no Consiliums, Freeholds, or Praxis to manage the more day to day affairs of those dwelling within the city, isolated as it is from the wider world.</i><br /> _______________________________________<br /> <br /> N\u00e4rwick is a crossover-centric Chronicles of Darkness setting I designed long ago, and have retooled for a 2nd edition crossover game. The characters are all part of a 'Pack' that acts as a sort of paranormal detective agency within the city. They're newly formed, in fact having just completed their first 'hunt', and are eager to make a living in the strange city.<br /> <br /> The characters, and a brief description, are as follows (note that as a house rule I allowed players to choose two half/minor templates instead of 1 full template if they desired):<br /> <br /> <b>Daniel Cooper </b>(<a href=\"http://i4.photobucket.com/albums/y115/falco1029/Daniel1_zpsy2adcmg6.png\" target=\"_blank\">Sheet p1</a>, <a href=\"http://i4.photobucket.com/albums/y115/falco1029/Daniel2_zpsxdppvi4j.png\" target=\"_blank\">Sheet p2</a>)<br /> <b>Type:</b> Werewolf, Rahu, Blood Talon<br /> A violent, abusive, alcoholic man who's nonetheless both incredibly useful in a fight and capable of tracking down nearly anything. He has a son that he knows full well he can't let into his life, but at the same time feels responsible for keeping him safe and taken care of in a dangerous city like this. Like most of the others, he's a native to the area, born and raised in the oppressive atmosphere that the city can force upon people like him.<br /> <br /> <b>Darcy Quinn</b> (<a href=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/files.d20.io/images/26096340/OhDYfm_Vc0Zw8iboPnWNZw/med.jpg?1481255119\" target=\"_blank\">Image</a>, <a href=\"http://i4.photobucket.com/albums/y115/falco1029/Darcy1_zpsaqltuasv.png\" target=\"_blank\">Sheet p1</a>, <a href=\"http://i4.photobucket.com/albums/y115/falco1029/Darcy2_zpsoxbwghts.png\" target=\"_blank\">Sheet p2</a>)<br /> <b>Type:</b> Wolf-Blooded Proximus, custom Dynasty<br /> A 'shaman' who's part of a fairly potent lineage of Proximi, who have, over the years, been intermingled with the blood of Werewolves, forming a family of healers, magic men/women, and worshipers of Luna. She runs a small occult shop in the same building as the agency, and is the &quot;older sister&quot; of Dolly (below). In addition, she's quickly formed a bit of a crush on Rex (also below).<br /> <br /> <b>Dolly Quinn </b>(<a href=\"https://thegirlwithadream.files.wordpress.com/2011/05/2010-2011-emo-hair-trends-gallery-34.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Cover Image</a>, <a href=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/files.d20.io/images/26274017/mO6FicEnaL70b4PBfOruCw/med.jpg?1481672695\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Image</a>, <a href=\"http://s4.photobucket.com/user/falco1029/media/Dolly1_zpsopfgfn5s.png.html?sort=3&amp;o=3\" target=\"_blank\">Sheet p1</a>, <a href=\"http://i4.photobucket.com/albums/y115/falco1029/Dolly2_zpsy9bsd8ef.png\" target=\"_blank\">Sheet p2</a>)<br /> <b>Type: </b>Demon, Destroyer, Inquisitor<br /> Originally an Angel sent by the God-machine to take out someone within the Quinn dynasty, having had a Cover woven for her as the sister of one of the younger members of that family, she's since fallen from the God-Machine's favor. She's a stealthy, subtle individual who keeps her nature (beyond 'clearly supernatural') secret from nearly everyone but Darcy (who knows the basic idea).<br /> <br /> <b>Rex Frank </b>(<a href=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/files.d20.io/images/26309619/Nmh0U_WI4lsXKIis-H5OHA/med.jpg?1481768209\" target=\"_blank\">Image</a>, <a href=\"http://i4.photobucket.com/albums/y115/falco1029/Rex1_zpsoupezmsd.png\" target=\"_blank\">Sheet p1</a>, <a href=\"http://i4.photobucket.com/albums/y115/falco1029/Rex2_zpsvefdrkgc.png\" target=\"_blank\">Sheet p2</a>)<br /> <b>Type:</b> Ghouled Lost Boy, Independent<br /> Formerly the ghoul of a distant Mekhet regnant, he's since lost track of her, unsure of if he's been abandoned or she's been somehow taken away from him. Feeling weak and out of control without her, it wasn't too hard to draw him into the Delta Protocol as a way to improve upon his capabilities even without regular access to vitae... and perhaps as a way to help him get a hold of more. Notably, he's the only non-native, having found his way into the city from Britain, where he used to work as an officer of the law.<br /> <br /> The characters have a Totem, <b>City Owl </b>(<a href=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/files.d20.io/images/26303735/OEPNgNWbTFOsvN5TznFc2w/med.jpg?1481756179\" target=\"_blank\">Image</a>, <a href=\"http://i4.photobucket.com/albums/y115/falco1029/Pack_zpsja3ol19h.png\" target=\"_blank\">Totem/Pack Sheet</a>), a quiet, intelligent, nocturnal spirit that feeds off the mysteries the 'Pack' is often so intent on investigating; it joined them upon the official formation of their Pack just a few days ago.<br /> <br /> _______________________________________<br /> <br /> So, here's the summary for our first session, which was a bit shorter than it will normally will be due to power outages and sickness among the group. Note that I don't plan to include much here, even in spoilers, that the players aren't aware of.<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 1: Finding Father</b><br /> <br /> We start off with the group in a fairly recently put together 'meeting room' in the small building that houses both the detective agency (including Rex's mundane branch of it) and Dolly's occult shop, talking over recent events and their plans as a new Pack. It's early october, a new moon, but in N\u00e4rwick that already means snowfall, the short spring and shorter summer quickly leading into a wintery stretch that lasts a majority of the year.<br /> <br /> Daniel's already on his third beer as he listens to the others, and City Owl is perched quietly in the corner in Twilight, listening curiously to the group. Rex, meanwhile, is looking through the recent news among less savory corners of the net, and stumbles across a murder in Aemilianus' Watchway, an anonymous message on the page stating 'Somebody crossed the boundary again'.<br /> <br /> Having a bit of experience with the city, he realizes this likely was caused by a Supernatural creature crossing the border into the Watchway, a district that's well known as being entirely under the control of an oddly powerful group of hunters, the Templars of St. Aemilianus. For the moment, that means there's not much they can do on the matter, as it would likely be a death sentence for them to get close enough to investigate further.<br /> <br /> It's at this point that Daniel (and only Daniel) is startled by the sudden sight of a young, scared looking woman and the feel of her hand on his arm. Despite her innocent appearance, he immediately feels his hair standing on end, as if backed into a corner by another predator, and while he doesn't know what, he knows she's not likely as harmless as she appears. Despite the odd stuffed toy dog she seems to be carrying with her.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Are you there?&quot;</i> she asks him with an uncertain look on his face, as if not quite sure he really is right there in front of her. Surprised, he asks who she is, only to be asked by the rest of the group who he's talking to. Worried that her new packmate is talking to air after only a few drinks, Darcy uses Supernal Vision to try and get a sense of anything magical that might be there, but is unable to spot anything.<br /> <br /> The woman then informs Daniel that 'Toby' said that he could help her, showed him to her, and asked if him and his friends might help her if she 'revealed herself' to them. Somewhat uncertain, Daniel nonetheless says yes, and her Obfuscation drops.<br /> <br /> After a few moments to gather their senses, the group questions the girl, asking her name ('Eva'), and why she's there. She informs them again that 'Toby' lead her to them, and shows them the toy when asked who it is. Uncertain about both her answer and her appearance in general, Rex uses his Uncanny Perception to get a better look at the girl, and is met with a flash of fangs and the familiar taste of Vitae in his mouth: a Vampire.<br /> <br /> Continuing on, Eva tells them all that she needs their help; 'Father' is coming after her again, and she needs to find someone that can get rid of him, or at least keep him away from her, because even if she hides, he always finds her. She promises that, in exchange, she'll 'find something' for each of them, something they need. Vague though the premise is, the group agrees to help her out so long as she signs a receipt of sorts saying she promises to 'pay' them when all is said and done.<br /> <br /> Finally, she gives them her address, noting her home as a likely place where he'd go to find her, and as they start to discuss things, she vanishes once again. The group then decides to drive out to that house with Dolly at the wheel. On the way, Darcy asks if Rex is doing anything next weekend and wants to go with her to the new club opening up in Dionysus row; <i>&quot;Do you like me, circle yes or no&quot;</i> is muttered by Dolly, who gets lightly smacked by Darcy in response. Rex amusedly agrees to go after that, despite initially seeming uncertain.<br /> <br /> (House description: )<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/files.d20.io/images/26485812/2NInA_DRvlxqZqDspVvbdg/med.jpg?1482202366\" target=\"_blank\">https://s3.amazonaws.com/files.d20.i...jpg?1482202366</a><br /> <br /> An old-looking house that's much better kept than it appears to be at first glance; all the mold and moss seems to be entirely on the outer walls, not causing any structural damage, the apparent cracks and weather worn damage are in fact an odd decor, and the cloudy looking windows are in fact simply designed that way.<br /> <br /> In front of the house is a small garden, filled mostly with bushes, but also with an array of different colored flowers that seems to bloom oddly well no matter what the time of year. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Arriving at the place, they're immediately put off, but proceed with their investigation anyway. While Darcy looks the place over with Supernal Vision, finding an odd overlay of the influence of Stygia and the Primal Wilds, Daniel slinks away and into Urhan form so he can take a look around the exterior of the bproperty. He doesn't catch any recent human scents, but does notice random, scattered signs of movement and passing. For whatever reason, however, he immediately decides they're of a mundane origin, and not worth their time ((due to a dramatic failure on Eye for the Strange)).<br /> <br /> Reporting that to the others, it becomes clear that they'll need to go inside to find out what's ACTUALLY going on. They head to the front door, and open it, finding it unlocked. Oddly, the area inside seems pristine and clean, if still perhaps of older construction. Knowing it's the smart thing to do in a creepy building, the group splits up to investigate, with Dolly and Daniel heading upstairs, and Darcy and Rex checking out the main floor.<br /> <br /> Upstairs, Dolly and Daniel find it oddly dark, even for the night time, and so each deal with it in their own way (Daniel shifts into Dahlu form, while Dolly takes on the Night Vision of her Demon Form). Despite a minor glitch on Dolly's part (she finds sparks forming from beneath her foot every three steps or so), they're able to see the three rooms on that floor: a bedroom, a bathroom, and a locked room. They decide to check the locked room first, with Dolly managing to shoehorn a 'lockpick' together to get the door open. Inside, they find a shelf of journals written by Evangeline, as well as what seems like a 'kennel' for Toby (there's no signs of any ACTUAL dogs there), complete with actual dog food and a water bowl, as well as a nice cage.<br /> <br /> They then check the bedroom, finding little more than odds and ends, and a closet filled with nice dresses, and note that the windows are boarded up and half painted over. Inside the bathroom, though, they find a peculiarity; the medicine cabinet's not empty, and indeed has fairly low grade medical supplies such as band-aids, painkillers, and antibiotic ointment, among other things, despite the fact that none of those would be of any use to a Vampire.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Darcy and Rex do a search around the main floor, which consists of a living room, kitchen, and dining room, all of which appear lightly used. The fridge notably has a single red-labeled but otherwise unbranded bottle of 'beer' inside, but they decide against messing with that (Darcy assumes it must be blood, no matter what it looks like at first glance). What's more interesting, however, is a door that's been painted and shaped to look like a part of the wall, something that would be very easy to miss. It too is locked, but being a PI, Rex has actual lock-picking tools and makes easy work of it.<br /> <br /> Downstairs, they find what looks like a medieval dungeon, a basement filled with torturous, blood covered implements and tools, a sight that shakes Rex to the core, and makes Darcy uneasy. They give the room a look over to be sure nothing's hidden down there, then head up to meet the other two, just about as they're similarly finishing their own search. They discuss it a bit, and realize they're not quite sure WHOSE blood is on the implements downstairs, and go to check.<br /> <br /> Old as the blood is, Rex, despite a brief initial consideration, realizes tasting it is likely both useless and dangerous, instead waiting as Darcy again relies on magical capabilities to try and discern a bit about it another way. She determines it's of a deathly origin, and thus is likely a Vampire's blood, not a person's, meaning it's quite likely, in their eyes, to actually be Evangeline's blood, not some victim's.<br /> <br /> They head back upstairs, then, to talk a bit more, but are interrupted as the area darkens, and a loud, deep, hate-filled voice cries out <i>&quot;EVANGELIIIINE!&quot;</i>, which immediately prompts some of them to get ready for oncoming danger. The voice repeats a bit louder each time until finally the shadows in the area begin to coalesce together, a semi-humanoid figure stepping 'out of' the nearby wall. Its eyes are glowing red, and its arm looks like it's been formed into a giant shadowy blade.<br /> <br /> Despite the foreboding sight (to those that can see it) of their Totem spirit flying off as the creature appears, the group initially tries to fight it off, but as Rex's blade passes straight through it without so much as making contact, they realize they'd be better off running. They turn to do exactly that, but the creature preys upon Rex's already shaken nature (given what he'd just gotten done seeing), and causes the ghoul to stumble over to the ground, giving it a chance to approach. Darcy immediately runs back, utilizing Body Control to both quicken Rex's reactions and toughen his flesh a bit as she starts to help him up. Dolly, meanwhile, appears to be running still, but in actuality uses Cause and Effect, her foot catching a loose board, knocking Rex back over but deflecting his sword into the creature's bladed arm, sticking it into the wall and giving them all a chance to get out of there.<br /> <br /> They take a brief moment to give the thing a better look (Via Supernal Vision and UNcanny Perception), but don't manage to learn much in the brief timeframe, other than the fact that the creature lacks a mana pool. Quickly, they all rush the rest of the way to the car, pile in, and Dolly floors it. In fact, she floors it a bit too hastily, and almost plows them all straight into a tree (&quot;Stop trying to kill us!&quot; ~Darcy &quot;If I wanted to kill you, you'd be dead!&quot; ~Dolly).<br /> <br /> End of Chapter<br /> <br /> ______<br /> <br /> <br /> So, if this is entertaining to anyone, I'll go ahead and try to do this again each week. I enjoy crossover games and hope that I'll get a chance to do some interesting stuff with it for my group, so we'll see how things go!<br /> <br /> Please feel free to post any questions/comments about it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 12-29-2016, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T06:28:18-08:00","id":1021964,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;Are you there?&quot;</i> she asks him with an uncertain look on his face, as if not quite sure he really is right there in front of her. Surprised, he asks who she is, only to be asked by the rest of the group who he's talking to. Worried that her new packmate is talking to air after only a few drinks, <b>she</b> uses Supernal Vision to try and get a sense of anything magical that might be there, but is unable to spot anything.<br /> <br /> Probably want to replace the bolded she with Darcy, for clarity's sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T10:22:59-08:00","id":1022029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021480-actual-play-chronicles-of-darkness-n\u00e4rwick?p=1021964#post1021964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;Are you there?&quot;</i> she asks him with an uncertain look on his face, as if not quite sure he really is right there in front of her. Surprised, he asks who she is, only to be asked by the rest of the group who he's talking to. Worried that her new packmate is talking to air after only a few drinks, <b>she</b> uses Supernal Vision to try and get a sense of anything magical that might be there, but is unable to spot anything.<br /> <br /> Probably want to replace the bolded she with Darcy, for clarity's sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T13:29:19-08:00","id":1022074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1021480-actual-play-chronicles-of-darkness-n\u00e4rwick?p=1022029#post1022029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good catch, thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're welcome. Any chance we can see character sheets on main characters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T13:53:55-08:00","id":1022082,"title":"","content":"Sure, I'll take some screenshots of their roll20 sheets (no easy way to save them otherwise) and place a link by their intros.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Done.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 12-25-2016, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T20:41:25-08:00","id":1027407,"title":"","content":"Session 2 was today! Dunno how many people are paying any attention to this, but hopefully someone's enjoying it!<br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 2: Case Closed</b><br /> The group arrived back at the building as snow's beginning to fall, rather late into the night now, knowing they'll need to regroup. Not terribly surprisingly, Evangeline is there again, inside, looking nervously towards them all as they head into the back room <i>&quot;You saw him, didn't you?&quot;</i> she asks, which they're all quick to confirm. <br /> <br /> They decided to try asking her a few questions, such as when Father first started causing her such direct trouble, and when she first moved into that place. Her answers are a bit wishy washy, at best, but they learn she's been there a few months, and that Father started bothering her shortly after she moved in there. And finally, that she lived with 'Grandfather' before then (<i>&quot;He's much nicer, though, don't worry&quot;</i>~Eva).<br /> <br /> The group finds the mentions of 'Grandfather' curious, and so decide to ask a bit about him, learning that he's a Vampire like her, and so unlike Father probably is more directly related in a way. They then ask if they can talk to 'Grandfather', to which she tells them she'll need to &quot;go ask him&quot;. Rather than disappearing this time, however, she simply closes her eyes and suddenly goes entirely limp in her chair, slumping downward. Daniel rushes over to help her, but can't get any reaction. Still, he feels that same predatory presence within her, and so knows her unlife hasn't been extinguished or anything. She also still has a very firm grip on Toby.<br /> <br /> While waiting for her to come to (and give an answer about if Grandfather will talk to them, however she's going about it), Rex and Darcy decide to do a bit of research, now that they have a bit more experience with what 'Father' actually is, or appears like, the former among the net and the latter in the library she has access to from her shop. Dolly decides to help her sister out, too.<br /> <br /> Darcy (with Dolly's help) manages to find information on a couple of relevant, if generally separate types of entities. Noting father's Shadowy form, she managed to find some vague mentions of the 'Owls of Dis', creatures of shadow that often come as an ill omen, and have some sort of connection to the undead. She also found some information about various types of Goetia that could perhaps be formed by certain types of mental trauma. Putting a few things together, the group came to their first theory that this 'Father' might be some form of modified Goetia taking a form similar to the Owls due to being formed from an Undead mind. <br /> <br /> At about that time, Eva rather gently comes to, looking around and getting the attention of the others. She tells them that Grandfather is on his way, which causes the group to react with some uncertainty, since they hadn't initially intended to invite him THERE, but they eventually just resign to waiting. Rex does take the time to finish his own research, however, and finds some stories that seem to coincide with what Darcy spoke of. On the bloggish sort of website of an apparent 'ghost hunter' in the city, there's talk of hauntings not caused by ghosts, sometimes seeming to be caused by extreme trauma due to a murder or similar happenstance, but wherein the spectre haunting the victim doesn't behave like a ghost typically should. There's been a few of these around town, often close to the Nexus. Notably, there's no name or contact info on the web page.<br /> <br /> He also spots a surprisingly quickly published publication from a fringe online 'paper', local to Narwick, talking about suspicious figures in the Stone Roost and the blood curdling screams emanating from the same house the group had gone to. Again, no actual name attached to it.<br /> <br /> While he does this, they ask Eva a bit more about Grandfather, and learn he's been around &quot;as long as the city itself&quot;, which made the group curious about N\u00e4rwick's actual age (none could recall). They decided to have Daniel check Wikipedia on his phone, but he found himself unable to actually concentrate on the page, the information slipping from his mind in a way that made him question how drunk he might be. The others didn't care enough to check themselves.<br /> <br /> Just as the group asks how long Grandfather will be, Evangeline gives a sudden &quot;He's here!&quot;, immediately followed by a knock on the door. Darcy goes to answer it, and is incredibly surprised to see Adrian Calahanz, the Elder who occupies the Vampiric seat of the supernatural Council that watches over the city (or at least keeps it at peace). He amusedly asks if Eva just referred to him as 'Grandfather', to which they confirmed. And a moment later, Eva is then clinging to her grandsire in greeting.<br /> <br /> Adrian is surprised to learn that 'Father' is still bothering her, apparently aware of the entity but having thought it was a one time thing since she hadn't said anything else. She admits to not wanting to have bothered him, busy as he so often is. Unfortunately, that also means that Adrian knows little more than the group, for the moment, about what exactly he is. With a bit of pressing, however, he does offer to check with his 'Contacts' if they have a private room he can use. Rex shows him to his own office, and gives him the privacy he asked for. Darcy mutters something about 'wards versus vampire', which Eva, despite being a distance away, overhears, and just simply says &quot;That wouldn't work on Grandfather&quot; (<i>Well from what I hear he's one of the good guys, to the extent a bloodsucking vampire can be&quot; </i>~Daniel.<br /> <br /> While he did that, Rex took some time to begin trying to hack into the site that published the story about them, to take it down, but is able to do little more than probe at security before Adrian comes back to the group. He walks up to Eva and says &quot;Tell me what happened a few months ago, dear&quot;, a concerned look on his face. Eva clutches Toby tightly, though, and refuses to talk to him about it. Despite continued pressing by him, she refuses to give in.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Darcy suggests to Daniel that he talk to the Vampiress, since he was the one she originally approached. He agrees to, and quickly enough notices how guilty she seems, and tries to reassure her that it's alright to talk to them about whatever it is. She agrees to tell HIM if Grandfather leaves, &quot;and promises not to <i>listen</i>&quot;. He's unsure at first, but since the group all say it's fair, he shrugs and decides to head off for now, busy as he is to begin with, and let them deal with her. Darcy escorts him out and asks what he found from his contacts, and he just vaguely tells her that if they can make her admit what she did, they'll find what they need to deal with Father.<br /> <br /> She also asks if he knows anything about Goetia, and oddly enough, he does seem to, giving the basic outline she already read through, that they're entities born of the mind, and asks if she can be more specific. She asks how they'd normally be fought, and he tells her that the same ways that can work on spirits, like exorcisms and such, can work on them, but there's no guarantee that will work in this case. <br /> <br /> As she returns to the rest of the group, and it's clear that Adrian is gone, Eva whispers to Daniel, &quot;<i>It was an accident... I was just so hungry...</i>&quot;, voice breaking a bit. He echoes the sentiment for the others, and Rex suggests she must have killed them to be so guilty about it, eliciting a deeper frown from her, and a repeated insistence that it was an accident.<br /> <br /> They ask about what happened, and with a bit of continued cajoling, piece together that in the throes of frenzy she ended up breaking into a pregnant woman's home and killing her. The same home that she now lives in. For whatever reason, she decided that as a sort of penance, she should watch over the place, make sure it's upkept, since she didn't know anything else about her victim, nor really how to look into them. She didn't remember much about it, but DID recall that &quot;Toby was there&quot;.<br /> <br /> After a bit of thought, Darcy decides to take a closer look at Toby, utilizing Pierce Deception to take a closer look at the mundane looking toy. She notices that is indeed supernatural, not some stuffed toy, and exudes a form of enhanced insight, but that said energy is somehow corrupted right now. Daniel similarly looks across the Gauntlet to see what essence or spirits might be attracted to the toy, and sees a few motes of corrupted insightful ephemera about it, feeding on whatever it's exuding (he also sees City Owl hiding out in the Shadow).<br /> <br /> With this final piece of the puzzle, everything starts to come together for them. Toby, a supernatural item that both clearly has a connection to Eva and expands on her own insights was with her when she did something terrible, killing and draining dry a pregnant woman after breaking into her home in the throes of frenzy. The terrible resonance that she created was not only reflected in Toby, but enhanced by him, creating a figure that represented her guilt and fear, in the form of an abusive 'Father', a mental projection tainted by the curse of undeath.<br /> <br /> Toby itself, then, likely has to be used for Father's downfall, and Daniel asks if they can speak privately, asking Eva to leave. Darcy's unsure about if she's actually gone after she heads out of the room, so utilizes Pierce Deception again, but doesn't see anything, so says they're likely fine to talk. Daniel then takes the time to point out that the most obvious means of solving this is likely destroying the toy. Rex warns that they likely wouldn't survive the ensuing frenzy that'd cause, though, and the group agrees that's likely not the best option.<br /> <br /> After discussing a few other possibilities, Darcy suggests trying to channel the corrupt essence out of the toy and into some other vessel. Not sure what else to do, the group agrees to try, and brings Eva back into the conversation, asking if they can try to help Toby.<br /> <br /> Darcy is able to successfully use her Blessing, drawing some twisted energy from Toby into a vessel, a little origami dog meant to work as a temporary storage for it. As she does, though, she catches Toby's eye, and undergoes a flash of insight. While that alone can't 'cure' Toby or destroy Father, that essence contains enough of a connection to the toy and to Eva to allow that origami doll to act as a sort of Talen, which will imbue the group and allow them to act as Father's Bane.<br /> <br /> Reassuring Evangeline that they'd soon take care of Father, they do mention they need to get some rest before they try, but Eva is nonetheless happy to hear it, and talks about how that gives her time to find what she promised them all. She heads off, as does most of the group, but Rex decides to take another hour or two to try and finish the job getting rid of that article, just for the sake of being safe. He's able to do so surprisingly easily and thoroughly, even leaving a bit of Spyware behind to try and get a bit more info about their apparent stalker.<br /> <br /> The next day, the Pack is quick to meet up to take care of Father, wanting to get it taken care of (though Darcy notably stops to get Rex some food on the way over). Daniel asks the Pack for help preparing the Siskur-Dah rite to empower them on their hunt for the entity, and they agree. The rite goes very smoothly, and upon its completion, the ENTIRETY of the pack feels renewed and invigorated, perhaps not as fully as the Uratha himself, but definitely a bit more than is typical for non-Wolves on the Hunt.<br /> <br /> They waste no more time, again driving off towards Eva's home, Darcy using the time to cast a bit of protective magic on the group (via Body Control). Daniel, meanwhile, looks at the house across the Gauntlet as they get closer, and sees a surprisingly large Magath there around the home, looking like a giant mosquito made up of heart muscle, pumping just like one would. A mixture of a Hunger and Blood spirit, Darcy guesses when he describes it to her.<br /> <br /> They get inside, set up an ambush, and then activate the 'Talen', feeling its corrupt essence uncomfortably <i>oozing </i>into their forms. At first, nothing happens, but within a short time, the room darkens, and a deep voice cries out &quot;You REEK of her!&quot;<br /> <br /> The shadows thicken, and Father steps into the home once more, but they're ready for him. Acting as the distraction, Rex readies his weapon as if to parry the shadowy blade wielded by the creature, only to keep it from seeing Daniel, in Urshul form, leaping out of his own Darkness. In two swift movements, the Uratha first severs the thing's smoky legs from its shadow body, throwing it to the ground, and then leaps for its throat, biting down and cutting off a distant scream as his essence-laden jaws clamp through Father's lifeforce.<br /> <br /> Father dies in a spectacular fashion, melting into a form of bloody, shadowy black ooze (<i>&quot;I would not suggest tasting him&quot;</i> ~Daniel, after some of it got in his mouth), and then boiling away in a black vapor. The Hunt complete, they all feel strengthened by it, and know that Father has truly been defeated.<br /> <br /> Relieved, but wanting to look a bit further into the room of horrors down below, they decide that, before they leave, they should investigate, only to find out that nothing they saw last night is there anymore. As best they can figure, those torturous implements were a further extension of Father, or whatever curse had infected Toby.<br /> <br /> As they're about to head out, Darcy feels herself torn across the Gauntlet all of a sudden, the Magath curious as to what just happened to make it &quot;taste better&quot; there (and her being a Waystone, she was the easiest target). She described it as best she could with her understanding of the Spirit Tongue, and seeming content enough, it says it's glad for that, and as such won't &quot;eat her&quot;, before sending her back across.<br /> <br /> Darcy immediately insists they all leave. On the way back, they stop to eat and to relax a bit, since it's still the early afternoon and Eva's not likely to be there until sunset.<br /> <br /> In fact, she arrives EXACTLY at sunset, already seated in a chair, leaving the group wondering if she managed to sleep there unseen somehow. She already seems to know Father is gone, and gives Dolly a hug, her being the closest one to show her emotion to. And she assures them that, as promised, she found something for all of them. There's suddenly a large bag at her side, which she reaches inside, asking who wants to get theirs first.<br /> <br /> Darcy volunteers first, and she's presented with a small black kitten, &quot;Toby says his name is Warlock, Master of the Arcane&quot;, sounding almost in disbelief at that name (but she'd never doubt Toby). She tells Darcy that he was chased out of his home by something bigger (<i>&quot;I don't know exactly what, I don't speak cat very well&quot;</i>) (&quot;<i> 'Very well...' &quot;</i> ~Rex) . The kitten, meanwhile, is purring and happy in Darcy's hands.<br /> <br /> Dolly volunteers next, and is given... a sandwich. But it's not just any sandwich; she can see the weaving of infrastructure within it, the product of some sort of Occult Matrix, perhaps. Curious, she takes a bit, and is then fairly quickly compelled to eat the rest. With each bite, she feels a bit of her Cover's memory relating to food sharpen and become more distinguished: the first time she had a cheese steak, Dolly's favorite types of foods, the way different flavors evoke different emotions, and she feels her Cover building as these otherwise mundane details are filled out. She asks Evangeline where she got it, and is simply answered with &quot;I found it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Next, Rex is given a vial of Vitae. &quot;Yours?&quot; he asks her, but she shakes her head and insists it's <i>his, </i>very notable enunciating the word. For now, he pockets it, not one to drink in front of his friends, and not currently hungry enough for his addiction to force it. <br /> <br /> Finally, Daniel is handed what looks like a bunch of used needles wrapped together in the form of a bracelet and covered with old, melted plastic. As soon as he touches it, though, he recognizes that it's a Fetish, and rather curious, he activates it. He immediately discovers it gives him control over Addiction itself, something that might help him with his own vices in the future. He too asks where she got it, but again is only answered with &quot;Like I said, I found it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thanking them one more time, and promising to send more business their way, she heads out, happy as ever, leaving the group to their devices. Darcy and Dolly head out to pick up some cat supplies, leaving Warlock with the others, handing him to Rex specifically. Unable to help himself, Rex utilizes Uncanny Perception to discern Warlock's nature; he spots thorny vines winding up and around the kitten's body, but never piercing it, and then as he seeks out if something else is controlling the feline, the vines burst away, making its freedom clear. Finally, he tries to get a sense of the kitten's mood, only to be drawn to its curious eyes and suddenly much louder purring. He doesn't know what to make of the first part, but knows it's no ordinary kitten, at least.<br /> <br /> Epilogue: Later on, before heading to bed, Rex decides to try that Vitae he was given. As the familiar taste passes over his tongue and down his throat, he suddenly feels a shiver of fear and a pang of pain and hunger: his sire's. Not only is he sure that she's somewhere within the city, but he feels a bit of her power within the blood, sharpening his ability with Auspex.<br /> <br /> <b>End of Chapter</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T11:08:54-07:00","id":1131789,"title":"","content":"So, I had stopped writing these out because I didn't think anyone was really reading them, but I decided to go back and do the next chapter, since i had it recorded, and if there's any interest, I can try to get things up to the current date with the current characters (Daniel and his successor have been replaced), and current sheets. There's been some interesting happenings including Demons, a local group of unique Hunters, Goetia, Spirits, dream-stalkers, the goblin market, a First Change, The Pure, various members of the Council, and much more!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 3: Poe's</b><br /> <br /> As Darcy and Dolly get back with supplies for Warlock, Rex shares what he had seen regarding Warlock, who seemed innocent and cute as ever. Darcy again used Supernal Vision, noticing that the kitten most closely reflected arcadia, as she saw little 'thorny' cracks in reality surrounding it as time slows down, feeling the magic coming more easily than normal as Warlock purrs happily. Even more curious now, she asked <i>&quot;Are you a Fae Cat?&quot;</i> and was met with an innocent-sounding meow.<br /> <br /> A bit more power is called upon so she can Speak with Animals, and this time says <i>&quot;You are a special little kitten, aren't you?&quot;</i> to which she gets a resounding <i>&quot;Yep&quot; </i>(<i>&quot;Typical Cat...&quot; </i>-Darcy, aside). Further conversation with the kitten divulges that he is indeed a 'Fae kitten', that he likes magic, was chased away from his home in 'the hedge' by a 'bigger, meaner cat', and most importantly, that he likes pink. A bit more casual conversation and they find their way to bed. <br /> <br /> The next day, Monday, is the day that Darcy planned to bring Rex to the new club that was opening (<i>&quot;Why does it open on Monday? Doesn't seem like good business&quot; ~ </i>Darcy). Having had little to do over the course of the day, things passed by seemingly quickly as they tended the shop and dealt with their other respective jobs, then Darcy and Rex headed out in the evening to the club, which they learned after the fact (Darcy hadn't checked; she simply wanted a date with Rex) was called Poe's. Dolly, meanwhile, decided to stay back and take care of Warlock.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/files.d20.io/images/27584446/y-55e9yXL1FvPHftEqEqSQ/med.png?1484792092\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> This club, located in Dionysus Row, is contained within a fairly large, Gothic structure, lit with hues of red and the occasional blacklight. It has an impressive spire at its top, and an all-too-real looking crow decoration over the doorway that seems to glare down at those approaching.<br /> <br /> Inside the building is a mish-mash of gothic near-satire, industrial dance areas, and out of the way bars and seating. The dress seems to vary from actual gothic attire, to satire thereof, to casual wear, to whatever else one might want; there's no apparent dress code.<br /> <br /> Those with a sense for it, however, notice the familiar pulsating Aether indicative of purposely-wasteful Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The line itself was fairly long, and it was obvious that they'd need to wait for several hours before going out. As they approach the line, Warlock pops up out of Darcy's purse, apparently having hidden away in there despite being left with Dolly. The latter gets a text informing her she didn't lose the new kitten.<br /> <br /> That dealt with, they wait in line until it's their turn to get in about an hour or so later. Heading inside, they look over the place, and take note of the DJ who seems to be playing for the night. Notably not dressed in anything approaching gothic attire, nor playing music that really fits the general atmosphere of the place.<br /> <br /> The pair go and find some drinks and a table, and enjoy the club for a little while. Darcy, curious as ever in this city, though, activates Supernal Vision, and (with the luck of a failed Spoofing) notices the club's DJ has an aura very similar to Dolly's, as well as the roiling, unsuppressed energy of the Aether seeming to best reflect his nature. Rex then attempts to use his Uncanny Perception on the man when Darcy explains this to him, but distracted by the club, he swears the man's nature reflects that of a Ghoul like himself.<br /> <br /> Darcy sends a message to Dolly, but the latter claims the aura must be a 'trick of the light'.<br /> <br /> They enjoy the music, the drinks, and some dancing for a little longer before they start to notice something odd: a few people seem to be getting a little -too- into the music, to the point of dancing themselves exhausted to the point of nearly passing out, and most of the people in there don't care. Darcy attempts to look across the Gauntlet with another Blessing, but paradox takes hold, and she feels herself weakened, as if torn away from Luna's gaze, a painful rash forming across her forehead as the spell fails to work.<br /> <br /> Rex, helping her off the dance floor, activates the Spirit's Touch to get a sense for if anyone in the area is under someone else's control, and notices strange wisps of energy emanating from the dancers and reaching upward into a sort of fog or cloud that's just out of 'reach'. The pair decides the DJ must be to blame, and start to think about how that might be possible, and they send a message to Dolly saying she should come down and help deal with the weird stuff going on at the club.<br /> <br /> Dolly, as she arrives, notices the infrastructure woven through the building, and the way that it seems to almost funnel its 'waste' into the DJ's station itself as he plays. By that time, they notice that more people are starting to collapse, and though they help a few, it's becoming clear that there's too many to keep up with. Oddly, they also notice the DJ looking over at them almost with concern in his eyes (which seem to be an odd blue color for a moment), though he doesn't stop what he's doing. Dolly also notices through her Aether sense that while there's clearly something going on with his eyes, he wasn't using any other sort of ability that's affecting a wider area, at least nothing that'd register to her senses.<br /> <br /> Darcy tries to share her Supernal Vision and look across the Gauntlet again, but both of those spells fail, worsening her blisters and rash and the feeling of separation from Luna. At that point, they try to call in a gas leak, but find the cell reception seems scrambled. They leave and try again, and manage to get through, able to get the building evacuated as they explain what happened in a way that makes it sound as mundane as possible, unsure how else to get people out of there safely.<br /> <br /> Later that night, Rex manages to find his way into the local hospital's database, finding out about the lack of diagnosis of the 'gas leak' victims, and learning a bit about some of them. The official story is they must have been 'overexhausted', despite the widespread nature of it, and they're being held for observation. <br /> <br /> That evening, Rex is startled awake by the sound of crackling energy and metal scraping on metal, and sees the figure of what looks like a cybernetic 'werewolf' spirit manifested in his room, which prompts him to quickly draw his weapon. It demands to know who the 'blood slave's' master is, and he, compelled by a power that forces him to tell the truth, explains that she's missing. He's then questioned about why he was at Poe's and what happened, seeming downright confused when he claims to have just been there on a date and didn't know what happened at Poe's, but assumed it was the DJ. Which the 'spirit' claims was not the case.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Ephemeral cover is a cool exploit</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> With that, the spirit vanishes, and before too long, there's a loud, insistent knock on the door. Unsurprisingly to Rex, it's the DJ, who claims the spirit was a 'friend' sent ahead of him. The explanation is of course believable. They learn that the DJ assumed that the 'blood slave' and those with him had something to do with what happened.<br /> <br /> They do share a bit of info about what they learned that had happened there, and the DJ (Timothy, they learn), offers to pay for them to figure out whatever DID happen in the club, if only because he's a bit too busy to go too much into it himself. He gives Rex his card and after a bit more questioning about what he knows, he then heads on his way. And mentions if he ever stops being 'between masters', that said master should be kept away from his club. Apparently he dislikes Kindred.<br /> To note, they also find out that the club opened on Monday because of some odd 'permit difficulties' that prevented it from opening a couple days before.<br /> <br /> As the others wake up, Rex tells them about the two visitors and what's happened. After some talking, they decide to find their way to one of the victims' home at the club who they'd sent home in a cab before the police and ambulances had arrived.<br /> Before that, though, Rex also decides to do some digging on the DJ, and finds that, well, there's not a large footprint for him online at all. Over the past 10 years or so there's basic mentions of him here and there, but that's about it. <br /> Finally, he also does some quick looking into their apparent stalker online, and Rex manages to find and take down a picture of Darcy in a story about the club.<br /> <br /> With that, they head to the aforementioned man's home in Domashnye Park, at the edge of the district closer to the downtown area. The man seems like he has the worst hangover in the world, half-dressed and very out of it. He seems confused about who they are and why they're there, which is reasonable, but he's having even more trouble processing that than normal. When they explain that they got him home and mentioned the club, he said it was the &quot;best club ever&quot; and that he was going back that night. And that all he remembers is that &quot;it was awesome&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Domashnye Park is a somewhat rural, mildly populated 'suburb' on the outskirts of N\u00e4rwick, near where the city diverges into the Dying Hills and the Black Forest. Those within are usually fairly friendly on the surface, but seem uncomfortable with anyone not local to the area staying for too long.<br /> <br /> Usually, this isn't an issue, as the lack of any real features, entertainment, or even basic stores means that the majority of passers through will be gone within a day or so. Some few stay more than that, of course, and most of the time it's no issue, but every once in a while you hear a rumor about someone that overstayed their welcome and never came back from their visit.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Darcy, hoping to get some insight into his physical state, utilizes Analyze Life, studying the man. She learns that he's still pretty healthy, but is physically drained and fatigued. That's about it though. A few more casual questions are asked, and they manage to convince him not to go back to the club tonight, instead waiting a couple of days because that's when Darcy will be there next (a bit of flirting used to make that seem like the more reasonable date).<br /> <br /> Their next stop is the hospital, hoping to talk to a doctor about what happened directly, but they happen upon a clerk who's in a very bad mood, and manage to make it worse to the point that he won't even point the group in the right direction. Not wanting to wander aimlessly, they head out for the time being, figuring their next step will be to go back to The Club that night and see what else they can figure out.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, they do try to question Dolly a bit about the DJ and related things, but don't manage to get much out of her. Dolly's a perfectly normal mortal, after all.<br /> <br /> <b>End of Chapter</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, on that note, do let me know if you guys want to see more at all. I don't have every session recorded so I can't promise to get this much detail for all of them, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}